        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Based on what you've shared:\n\n- **Medication:** Semaglutide\n- **Concentration:** **2.5 mg/mL**\n- **Prescribed dose:** **0.2 mg**\n\nThe calculation is:\n\n- 0.2 mg \u00f7 2.5 mg/mL = **0.08 mL**\n\nOn your **0.5 mL (50-unit) insulin syringe**:\n- **50 units = 0.5 mL**\n- Therefore, **0.08 mL = 8 units**.\n\nSince your syringe is numbered every 5 units (10, 15, 20, etc.), **8 units is two small tick marks before the \"10\" mark**, assuming each small tick represents 1 unit (which is standard on most U-100 insulin syringes).\n\nSo you would draw up **8 units (0.08 mL)**.\n\nIf you want, you can also upload a photo of your syringe, and I'll point to the exact line you should fill to."
          ]
        },
