          "parts": [
            "Thanks for clarifying.\n\nIf your prescription is:\n\n- **Dose:** 0.2 mg\n- **Concentration:** 2.5 mg/mL\n\nThen the calculation is:\n\n- 0.2 mg \u00f7 2.5 mg/mL = **0.08 mL**\n\nOn a **50-unit (0.5 mL) U-100 insulin syringe**:\n- **0.08 mL = 8 units**\n\n**So you would draw the medication up to the 8-unit mark** (the 8th notch if each small marking is 1 unit).\n\nIf you tell me **the name of the medication** (for example, semaglutide or another medication), I can double-check that this matches the prescribed concentration."
