    "dca96551-41ab-4cbf-972b-c6758c317912": {
      "id": "dca96551-41ab-4cbf-972b-c6758c317912",
      "message": {
        "author": {
          "name": null,
          "role": "assistant"
        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Thanks for uploading the photos. I can read the prescription label clearly.\n\nYour prescription says:\n\n- **Semaglutide**\n- **Strength:** 2.5 mg/mL\n- **Dose:** 0.2 mg\n- **Directions:** **\"Withdraw and inject 8 units subcutaneously once weekly for 4 weeks.\"**\n\nSo the pharmacy has already done the calculation for you.\n\nOn your syringe:\n- **Draw the plunger to the 8-unit mark.**\n- Since your syringe is labeled every 5 units (5, 10, 15, etc.), **8 units is the second small tick mark below the \"10\"** (assuming the small ticks are 1 unit each, which they are on standard U-100 insulin syringes).\n\nYou're using the correct syringe, and **8 units** is the correct amount for your first weekly dose based on the prescription shown.\n\nOne tip: when measuring, line up the **top (needle-side) edge of the black rubber stopper** with the **8-unit** mark, not the bottom edge of the stopper.\n\nYou've got the right dose: **8 units once a week for 4 weeks.**"
          ]
        },
        "create_time": 1784248697.825033,
        "id": "dca96551-41ab-4cbf-972b-c6758c317912",
        "metadata": {
          "content_references": [],
          "model_slug": "gpt-5-5",
          "parent_id": "56af1625-b7f3-4b95-b6e7-8c1e13f59652"
        }
      },
