    "e1e49f6a-bf8d-4a86-bd97-e5d483c60b7b": {
      "id": "e1e49f6a-bf8d-4a86-bd97-e5d483c60b7b",
      "message": {
        "author": {
          "name": null,
          "role": "assistant"
        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "I want to make sure I don't accidentally tell you the wrong dose, because the way it's written is ambiguous.\n\nCan you tell me exactly which of these your prescription says?\n\n- **Dose:** 2 mg\n- **Concentration:** 2.5 mg/mL\n\nIf that's correct, then:\n\n- 2 mg \u00f7 2.5 mg/mL = **0.8 mL**\n- On a U-100 insulin syringe, **0.8 mL = 80 units**. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search1\ue202turn0search0\ue201\n\nA syringe with **50 notches (50 units/0.5 mL)** only holds **0.5 mL**, so **80 units will not fit in that syringe**. \ue200cite\ue202turn0search1\ue202turn0search0\ue201\n\nPlease either:\n1. Upload a photo of the prescription label, **or**\n2. Type exactly what the label says (including the drug name, strength, and directions).\n\nI'll calculate the exact line you should draw to."
          ]
        },
